 "summary": "Commodities were broadly weaker in the latest session, with 9 of the 24 tracked benchmarks higher and 14 lower. Energy was mixed, 2 of 4 higher, the biggest move coming from Petroleum (WTI) at +2.59% to 97.55 USD/Bbl; precious metals were mixed, 4 of 5 higher, the biggest move coming from Rhodium at -3.95% to 8500.00 USD/t oz; base metals fell across the board, led by Tin at -2.55% to 50446 USD/T; bulk and battery materials were mixed, 2 of 5 higher, the biggest move coming from Rare Earth Elements at +4.16% to 41.61 USD/share; agriculture was mixed, 1 of 4 higher, the biggest move coming from Sugar at +1.44% to 21.14 USd/Lbs. The largest single move across the complex was Rare Earth Elements at +4.16%. Coal (Newcastle), Tin have not refreshed past the prior day's print and are flagged accordingly, being fixed periodically rather than traded continuously. Rare earths are represented by the MP Materials equity proxy, as no reliable daily spot benchmark is published. Reported alongside the session, Business Standard on 15 October 2026:",
